<para>Watch this video to see how to divide expressions with exponents.</para>
<media alt="Placeholder for Alt Text"><iframe width="660" height="371.4" src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/AR1uqNbjM5s;&amp;rel=0"/></media>
</section>
<section>
<title>Videos</title>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>

    <para>\(\frac {x^4y^2z^5}{x^6yz^3}\)</para>
        <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  
  </problem><solution>
<para>Compare your answer:</para>

<para>\(\frac {x^4y^2z^5}{x^6yz^3}=\frac {y^{2-1}z^{5-3}}{x^{6-4}}=\frac {yz^2}{x^2}\). To divide with like bases, subtract the exponents.</para>

</solution></exercise>
</example><example><exercise>
  <problem>

    <para>\(\frac {x^9}{x^3}\)</para>
        <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  
  </problem><solution>
<para>Compare your answer:</para>

<para>\(\frac {x^9}{x^3}=x^{9-3}=x^6\). To divide with like bases, subtract the exponents.</para>



</solution></exercise>
</example></section>
